These defaults come from the LLMD source reviewed on 16 November 2026.

# [Estimate workload demand]($heading.id('page-estimate'))

Estimate logical KV-cache pages for full-length sequences in one data-parallel
group, with the default 16 tokens per page and before page reuse. The estimate
describes demand. Actual capacity depends on the model, backend, and device
memory. LFM3 uses one data-parallel group in the reviewed build.

```=html
<div class="cli-workload" data-cli-workload>
  <fieldset class="cli-workload-inputs" data-workload-inputs hidden data-pagefind-ignore>
    <legend>Workload</legend>
    <label class="cli-reference-field">
      Active sequences <span>1–16</span>
      <input type="number" name="sequences" min="1" max="16" step="1" value="1" required aria-describedby="cli-workload-error">
    </label>
    <label class="cli-reference-field">
      Tokens per sequence <span>1,024–32,768</span>
      <input type="number" name="context" min="1024" max="32768" step="1" value="4096" required aria-describedby="cli-workload-error">
    </label>
  </fieldset>
  <p class="cli-workload-error" id="cli-workload-error" role="alert" hidden></p>
  <div class="cli-workload-results" data-workload-results>
    <output data-workload-report aria-live="polite"><strong data-workload-pages>256</strong> estimated logical pages</output>
    <p class="cli-workload-equation" data-workload-equation>1 × ⌈4,096 tokens ÷ 16 tokens/page⌉</p>
    <p>Apply these overrides to your LLMD command in place of any existing values.</p>
    <div class="command-shell">
      <span class="command-language">LLMD overrides</span>
      <pre><code class="sh" data-workload-flags data-copy-label="Copy LLMD workload flags">--batch-size=1 --max-context-len=4096</code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

For example, four sequences of 4,096 tokens each need 1,024 logical pages.

# [Batching and cache defaults]($heading.id('batching-context-and-memory'))

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--batch-size=<requests>` | `16` | Limit concurrent requests in a batch. |
| `--token-batch-size=<tokens>` | `1024` | Limit the number of tokens processed in one inference step. |
| `--max-context-len=<tokens>` | `128000` | Set the server context cap. Check the model’s context length and the memory available. |
| `--prefill-chunk-size=<tokens>` | `256` | Limit the prefill chunk for each sequence. |
| `--page-chunk-size=<tokens>` | `16` | Set the number of tokens per KV-cache page. |
| `--gpu-memory-fraction=<fraction>` | `0.9` | Set an allocator limit on CUDA, ROCm, oneAPI, and Metal. Accepted values are greater than `0` and at most `1`. |
| `--cache-memory-fraction=<fraction>` | `0.95` | Scale the smallest reported per-device memory limit. The cache planner subtracts fixed allocations before sizing pages. Accepted values are greater than `0` and at most `1`. |

# [Parallel work and Decision requests]($heading.id('parallel-work-and-decision-requests'))

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--data-parallel=<groups>` | `1` | Set the number of groups that share request and KV-cache work in supported configurations. |
| `--systemone-window=<requests>` | Batch size divided by four, rounded down with a minimum of one | Limit the questions in flight within one [Decision request]($link.page('llmd/reference/v1/systemone').ref('decision')). |

The [20261106.0 release notes](https://zml.ai/posts/llmd-20261106.0/#data-parallelism-beta)
describe data parallelism on Llama as a beta feature.

# [Asynchronous scheduling]($heading.id('scheduling-and-attention-workers'))

Availability can vary by model, backend, and release.

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--async-scheduling` | Off | Enable asynchronous scheduling on supported models. The initial beta covers Llama and Gemma 4 without speculative decoding. |
